cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below. See docs/provenance.md for how to cite the underlying datasets, which are separate from this repository."
title: "pod-engagement-profile: aggregate-only companion analysis of engagement-pod datasets"
type: software
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-12
abstract: >
  A de-identified, aggregate-only companion analysis of three
  engagement-pod-adjacent datasets (podawaa2024, HyperClaper,
  LinkBoost-2025), oriented around 16 CFR 465.8 ("Misuse of fake
  indicators of social media influence"). No script or document in this
  repository identifies an individual account, author, or record; all
  reported figures are population-level statistics reproducible from the
  checksummed source files. See README.md and docs/ for method, data
  dictionary, limitations, privacy, provenance, and regulatory context.
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "LinkedIn posts using fake socials"
    authors:
      - name: "Daniel Hall"
    repository: "https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/WD9AUR"
    identifiers:
      - type: doi
        value: "10.7910/DVN/WD9AUR"
    notes: >
      Corresponds to podawaa2024.json in this repo (CORROBORATED via
      matching sha256 — see docs/provenance.md). HyperClaper.json and
      LinkBoost-2025.json are not part of this Dataverse record; see
      docs/provenance.md for their reported, STATED sources.
